<a2ui>
root=ColumnWave([a,d,i,o,v,ac,ai],gap="md",padding=16)
a=Column([b,c],"sm")
b=Text("What to keep as evidence","h2")
c=Text("Save the order confirmation, invoice/bill, product listing screenshots, and payment proof.\nTake photos or videos of the defect, ideally during unboxing, and keep the packaging, labels, and accessories.\nPreserve all emails, chat logs, complaint ticket numbers, pickup receipts, and return/refund status updates.\nIf the product was inspected or repaired, keep any job sheet or written service report.",variant="body")
d=Card([e])
e=Column([f,g,h,i],gap="md",padding=16)
f=Text("First complaint: seller and platform","h2")
g=Text("Report the defect immediately in writing through the app, email, or seller support, and clearly ask for refund, replacement, or repair.\nIf the marketplace route fails, escalate to the platform’s grievance officer/nodal contact and include the order number, defect details, evidence, and the exact remedy sought.",variant="body")
h=Text("Under current consumer guidance, platform-side redressal should be triggered quickly; some guidance cites a 72-hour response expectation for defective goods, but this should be treated as a platform-facing service timeline rather than a guaranteed statutory remedy window.","caption")
i=Card([j])
j=Column([k,l,m],gap="md",padding=16)
k=Text("Official grievance channels","h2")
l=Text("Use the National Consumer Helpline (NCH) as the pre-litigation escalation step; official consumer guidance lists 1915 as the toll-free helpline, with online and app-based complaint options.","caption")
m=Text("File the grievance with enough detail so the complaint can be forwarded and tracked: seller name, platform name, order ID, issue summary, evidence list, and the remedy requested.","caption")
n=Card([o])
o=Column([p,q,r],gap="md",padding=16)
p=Text("Escalation if the issue is not resolved","h2")
q=Text("If the seller/platform does not resolve the matter, file a complaint on e-Daakhil for the appropriate Consumer Commission. Choose the commission based on the value and jurisdiction of the claim; current consumer-law guides direct consumers to the District, State, or National Commission through the online filing system.","caption")
r=Text("In the complaint, name both the seller and, where relevant, the platform, and request refund/replacement/repair, compensation, and costs.","caption")
s=Card([t])
t=Column([u,v,w],gap="md",padding=16)
u=Text("Deadlines and timing","h2")
v=Text("The consumer complaint limitation period is generally 2 years from the cause of action under the Consumer Protection Act framework and related guidance.\nAct as soon as the defect is discovered, because delay can weaken evidence and make platform reversals harder to obtain.\nIf you paid by card and the refund is wrongly withheld, some consumer guidance notes that a bank chargeback may be tried in parallel, subject to your card issuer’s timelines.","caption")
w=Column([x,y,z],"sm")
x=Text("Practical approach","h2")
y=Text("Keep the defective item safe until the dispute is resolved, because the seller or platform may require inspection or return.\nUse written communication only where possible, since a clear paper trail helps at every escalation stage.\nIf the seller offers only store credit or a voucher for a clearly defective product, you can still press for the statutory remedy you want through the grievance and consumer-forum process.","caption")
z=Button("Continue","primary",on
</a2ui>